        "text": "We've learned how smart contracts and dapps make decentralized transactions and applications possible. The next level of complexity comes in the form of a decentralized organizational structure. This is where a decentralized autonomous organization, or DAO, in short, comes in. A DAO is an organizational structure or substructure commonly used for DApps, blockchain projects, sociopolitical funds, and crypto investment funds. With no central authority, token holders of a DAO collectively cast votes for the management of the dao. All votes are posted on a blockchain for public viewing. Because of their decentralization and transparency, as well as their ability to work with self executing smart contracts, DAOs have become a popular governing method in the blockchain and crypto space.",
        "start": 2960,
        "end": 49310,
